# The hook at every boot: TOS sets its vectors again at a reset and starts
# GEMDOS's memory afresh, and the user firmware (the sentinel keeps
# CMD_START) installs the hook again, in memory it takes anew. After a
# warm reset the vectors reach it once more and its counters start at 0.
@printer
@disk-a tools/dev/builds/disks/autotest.st
text "Machine +: (ST|STE|Mega STE), TOS" 1500
key e
wait 100
key 0x01
screen same autotest 1500
hookstate first
reset warm
newlog "Setting shared variable 1 to" 1500
wait 100
key 0x01
screen same autotest 1500
hookstate again
key 0x39
desktop 2500
